# One variable per pool, prefixed with its name: a fine-grained or classic PAT
# with self-hosted-runner write (administration:write) on that *organisation* —
# the image self-mints short-lived registration tokens from it, so registration
# survives restarts without manual token refresh. Org-scoped runners are
# offered to every repository of that organisation, so the pools are kept
# apart by label rather than by scope, and the PAT is scoped to the
# organisation rather than to a repository.
#
# A fine-grained PAT covers one owner, so each organisation needs its own; a
# classic PAT of a user who admins both organisations may be pasted in both.
#
# Set every one: while any is empty, the whole stack fails to deploy and the
# running pools stay as they are. Leave nothing after an empty `=`: an
# unquoted "# …" there is read as the value, and gets past that check.

TICKIFY_ORG_ACCESS_TOKEN=

NOBINALO_ORG_ACCESS_TOKEN=
